00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:04,960
Well, there's something that I look for in consumer apps and trying to understand why they've been so successful.

232
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:17,440
I look at ones like Ladder or Altrails or Strava, and I think that they all associate with a person's identity something that they repeat frequently, whether it's like running or weightlifting.

233
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:27,600
And to us, we felt like we were capturing a student's identity and going to class and recording is something you do daily or a few times a week.

234
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:35,360
And that was a big thing for us is trying to find something that not just brings value, but you do it like in an often and repeated way.

235
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,840
And you build up this like also just this corpus, right, over time, right?

236
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:45,600
Of like, you know, especially if like subsequent classes like physics one, two, three, you can now go back and reference physics two.

237
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:47,200
You get all this like lock-in, right?

238
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,640
Which is really.

239
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:51,280
They're just going to be really powerful in terms of retention and things like that.

240
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:52,000
Totally.

241
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,600
Let's dive into growth.

